---
title: "Introduction to Grant Proposal Writing"
code: "BUS-140"
category: "business-management-and-administration"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Introduces the complete process of grant proposal development. Focuses on identifying achievable and fundable projects and preparing a full proposal package for submission. Presents strategies to seek external grant funding from private, community, and corporate foundations. Lecture 3 hours per week.
